        "date_published": "2026-09-27T23:10:57+00:00",
        "description": "<p>And I don't mean the doomerism nonsense. From rogue AI, doomerism, AGI.<p>I mean real regulation:<p>1) Fair accounting of input/output tokens. Where is the weights and measures department to enforce  fair counting of usage? If I pay for a gallon of gas, that is what I expect. When I pay for a dollar of LLM compute, is it going to play games with the input (or especially the output) tokens to devalue my dollar?\n2) Quality. When I request a higher effort of a frontier model, and then I get downgraded to a lower tier model or with different effort levels (and I may not even know if I was downgraded!), they are effectively selling you a service you didn't ask for. \"But the terms of service\", great, if they feel it is such a risk to downgrade, and they get it wrong a lot, then they should discount the cost of the downgraded response.\n3) Adulterating outputs. LLMs are now routinely adulterating output for tracking and accountability purposes, but is there anyone to validate these efforts",
